   $q$Which statement about $0.7$ and $0.007$ is true?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$0.7$ is $1000$ times as much as $0.007$.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"counted-all-three-decimal-places"},{"text":"$0.007$ is $100$ times as much as $0.7$.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reversed-the-relationship"},{"text":"$0.7$ is $10$ times as much as $0.007$.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"moved-only-one-place"},{"text":"$0.7$ is $100$ times as much as $0.007$.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$0.7$ is $100$ times as much as $0.007$.$q$, $q$The $7$ in $0.7$ is in the tenths place and the $7$ in $0.007$ is in the thousandths place. Moving from thousandths to tenths is two places to the left, and each place is $10$ times the one to its right, so $10 \times 10 = 100$. Check: $0.007 \times 100 = 0.7$. The choice saying $1000$ times counts the three decimal places of $0.007$ instead of the places between the two digits.$q$, 'draft', null)
